# Open-source research

- Stars ≠ quality. Evaluate architecture, tests, maintenance, license.
- **Do not copy** AGPL/GPL application code (e.g. wger, openfoodfacts-server).
- Safe reuse examples: MIT/Apache/Unlicense libraries and datasets (Dexie, zxing, free-exercise-db) with attribution.
- Before adopting a dependency: record license, commit/branch, safe vs study-only in research notes.
- Prefer official API docs (USDA, OFF, Supabase, Next.js) over blog summaries.
- Label uncertain findings explicitly.
- Study wger/OFF for domain ideas only; implement original code in this repo.
